diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 29bbc8f..2bbc915 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
 
 ## Unreleased
 
+- Fixed: conversions used binary floating point, so `0.235 m` in `cm` rounded as 23.499999999999996 and printed `23 cm` at precision 0. Conversions now use exact decimal arithmetic.
 - Compound units in results are written with a middle dot and superscript powers, as in `kg·m²/s²`; both forms are accepted as input.
 - `unitconv list` shows 20 units a page, with `--page N` and a `page N of M` footer.
 - `--json` output gives `unit` as an object with the unit's `symbol` and singular `name`.
diff --git a/docs/reference.md b/docs/reference.md
index 366d5f9..5215cda 100644
--- a/docs/reference.md
+++ b/docs/reference.md
@@ -24,7 +24,7 @@ command-line options, each overriding the one before.
 | Fact | Value | Meaning |
 |---|---|---|
 | `convert.result` | `exact` | `convert()` returns the exact value; `format_quantity()` rounds it to `precision` places with the `rounding` mode |
-| `arithmetic` | `float` | numbers are binary floating point while converting |
+| `arithmetic` | `decimal` | numbers are exact decimals while converting, so `0.235 m` is `23.5 cm` before rounding |
 | `lookup.case` | `exact` | unit symbols match only as spelled, so `Mm` is megametres and `mm` millimetres |
 | `prefixes` | `G, M, k, h, da, d, c, m, u, n` | SI prefixes accepted before units that take them |
 | `table.version` | `2026.3` | version of the generated unit table |
